:: Farm Walk Back to Town [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 60>>
You sigh as you begin walking back to town, hardly even seeing the city from this distance. <span style="color:lightcoral">The walk is long and hard, the path alongside the road not paved and littered with rocks, inclines, and unstable footing. You nearly trip a few times and get your leg stuck in a bush when you have to pull away from the road due to a puddle.</span> You have no idea how people used to travel like this before cars. <br>
<br>
It takes a lot longer than you’d like, and you feel rather exhausted by the end of it, but you eventually see your destination in sight! The visual of the Preston High School only about half a mile away gives you the energy you need to get through the final push. You cheer to yourself as you make it back to town… then immediately have to take a seat on the sidewalk to rest your feet. <span style="color:yellow">Next time, you should really just take the bus.</span> <br>
<<needChange "Energy" -10>>
<br>
[[Continue|High School]]


:: Farm Walk To Farm [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 60>>
Walking past the high school, you begin your long trek out into the farmlands that border the eastern side of Opal City. <span style="color:lightgreen">At first, the walk is relaxing. Cool breeze, quiet roads, and the occasional instance of spotting an animal or two. It is pretty nice…</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:lightcoral">Until you’ve been walking for over 10 minutes. Then it starts to get a little annoying. Then tiring. Then, as you only just see your destination another mile ahead of you in the distance and the realization that you still have to go back to town at some point makes you sigh in exhaustion.</span> By the time you arrive, you collapse on the bench at the bus stop, really wondering why you decided not to take the bus. <br>
<<needChange "Energy" -10>>
<br>
[[Continue|Farm]]

:: Farm Bike To Farm [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 30>>
Standing at the path that leads down to the farming area, which you can only see the beginning of miles away, you are pretty happy that you have a bike to make the journey easier. Hoping on, you begin your journey. Sadly, said journey has a lot of uphill parts that start to tired and wear you out. The only up side is thinking how easy the ride back will be. <br>
<br>
It takes about 30 minutes to arrive and you come to a stop just by the bus stop. Sure, taking the bus may have been easier. <span style="color:lightgreen">But this way was cheaper and probably much more fun! You feel pretty energized after such a trip!</span> <br>
<<needChange "Energy" -5>>
<<needChange "Fun" 5>>
<br>
[[Continue|Farm]]


:: Farm Bike Back to Town[nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
You begin your ride home, thankful that you have a bike when the tip of the buildings seem to far away. <span style="color:lightcoral">The ride back is actually pretty easy compared to the ride there, as most of it is downhill and outside of getting off the road to avoid the few cars coming by, it is relatively uneventful.</span> Once you arrive back at the high school, you take a second to stretch your legs before continuing onwards. <br>
<<needChange "Energy" -2>>
<<needChange "Fun" 5>>
<br>
[[Continue|High School]]
